# **Snake City: traps, puzzles, combat, Soul Clan and movement — an engineering design**

The strongest direction for Snake City is to make it feel like a **living mechanical-fantasy world**, not simply a game where a serpent walks around, fights enemies and collects items.

Think of the player as an evolving organism operating inside an ancient world built from forgotten machines, energy systems, biological mechanisms and intelligent factions.

The central design principle should be:

**Every trap is a mechanism. Every puzzle is a system to understand. Every fight is a problem of timing, positioning and resource management. Every movement skill changes how the player interacts with the world.**

I'll break it down as a game designer and a mechatronics engineer.

