The environment should contain several interacting systems:

- Mechanical systems: gears, pistons, pressure plates, counterweights, elevators and rotating platforms.
- Electrical or energy systems: power nodes, conductive paths, energy barriers and overloaded circuits.
- Fluid systems: water channels, hydraulic lifts, pressure pipes and movable gates.
- Biological systems: vines, roots, poisonous spores, living walls and creatures that react to sound or heat.
- Ancient technology: portals, soul-powered machines, artificial guardians and forgotten control systems.

This gives you a way to build puzzles that are not arbitrary. The player observes a mechanism, develops a hypothesis, tests it and learns how the world works.

